Date: 22 Sep 1994 05:49:04 GMT
Message-ID: <35r5sg$kec@vixen.cso.uiuc.edu>


Q: Will content of the infobahn be regulated by the Canadian government ?
 
It may be worth considering the recent response by the CRTC
to complaints about campus radio station CKDU-FM at Dalhousie University.
 
Principle among the complaints seems to be explicit homosexual subject matter.
 
In the vague wording of the Broadcasting Act, from which the CRTC
derives its mandate, Paragraph 3(1) (g) states:
 
        "the programming originated by broadcasting undertakings
        should be of high standard".
 
Apparently the CKDU-FM program "All Day, All Gay", aired to celebrate
gay and lesbian pride day, may not have been of sufficient "high standard",
or at least not enough that it could be aired before 9pm.
 
Q: Is one's right to freedom of expression unreasonably limited
   if one is only allowed to speak under cover of darkness?

 
