If this is not the appropriate place for this or if
it's old hat, I apologize, but I've been off the Net
for awhile.

Today's New York Times (front page) has an interesting
little piece about Santa Rosa Junior College and a 
settlement reached with 3 students who filed a lawsuit
against the college because of Title IX violations that
occurred on a computer bulletin board.  The boards in
question were male-only and female-only sites, where
one of the plaintiffs (a woman) was spoken about in an
unfavorable way by the male users.  It was declared
sexual harassment by the Dept of Ed Office of Civil
Rights.  Mike Godwin of EFF was quoted in the article.

While I do not in any way condone sexual harassment,
two good issues were raised:

1.  Freedom of association 
2.  Freedom of speech
Would love to hear comments from others who have
seen the NY Times article.  It seems to me to be
the first time that a federal agency has actually
found a way to regulate content on a bbs, which I find
very distressing.

Marianne Goodland
